location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify that `ensure-pandoc` gates on the decoded ARCHITECTURE of the resolved pandoc (not mere presence of a file/PATH binary), so a stale wrong-arch `.tools/bin/pandoc` or an unrelated PATH pandoc still triggers repair, unlike the presence-based actionlint-bin template.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.466,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["actionlint-bin skips when `command -v actionlint` or `[ -x $(LOCAL_BIN)/actionlint ]` (Makefile:468-472) — presence, not architecture","Plan: 'triggered by an architecture mismatch rather than a platform name'","Plan: 'On a mismatch it downloads ... installs it to ... .tools/bin/pandoc' — but the Makefile wrapper's skip condition is unspecified"],"finding":"The ensure-pandoc Makefile target is modelled on actionlint-bin (Makefile:467-483), whose skip logic is PRESENCE-based (`command -v actionlint` / `[ -x .tools/bin/actionlint ]`), but the plan's stated trigger is an ARCHITECTURE MISMATCH, not presence. The plan does not specify how the Makefile target reconciles these: a presence-based short-circuit would skip repair when a wrong-arch .tools/bin/pandoc already exists (e.g. a stale/partial install) or when an unrelated pandoc is on PATH, re-introducing the defect the ticket removes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f175c7ddf601f5c67","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: Makefile new `ensure-pandoc` target; Approach (arch-mismatch trigger)","norm_id":"nb22547175fd97f5c","priority":0.134,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A prior failed/partial install left an x86_64 binary at .tools/bin/pandoc; a presence-based target skips re-repair","An arm64 pandoc exists on PATH via Homebrew; a `command -v`-style guard short-circuits before the arch-mismatch check runs"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Have `ensure-pandoc` always invoke `scripts/ensure_pandoc.py`, which itself decides (arch match -> exit 0, mismatch -> repair), rather than reusing actionlint-bin's `command -v`/`[ -x ]` presence short-circuit in the recipe.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"eb9210f6a5ab54f6","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["d61429ea5eea1984",7358],"description_boxes":["83b7db61ca197115",0],"file_impact":["566d69383755bd63",6],"ticket_id":["c929169efba36e37",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":292593,"cache_write_tokens":105883,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":3715.1,"input_tokens":419020,"llm_calls":27,"llm_ms":111990.2,"output_tokens":21216,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":123237.6,"verify_requests":6},"model":